                                                "sense_id": "377d0ff0-abf8-3ef4-bcf3-d0808d695532",
                                                "text": "c. 1648, Walter Montagu, Devout Essaies.\nThe soul of man then is capable of a state of much peace and equanimity, in the exterior bands and agitations; but this capacity is rather an effect of the expropriation of our reason, then a vertue resulting from her single capacity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
